ink  he's going to run again  and i'm all for that i  will do everything i can to ensure  uh that uh the former president never  again gets anywhere near the oval office  when you can't have the republican  conference chair the republican party  spokesperson  consistently attacking the leader of the  party who 74 million americans  voted for in your party there's a large  conversation about cancel culture  has liz cheney been cancelled i've never  called for her  step down and and excuse me resigned  from congress i do think there's a big  difference though  between whether you're going to be in  congress or not and  us deciding as republicans in congress  who's going to be our spokesperson  trump has described cheney as a war  monger and yesterday called her a bitter  horrible human being is liz cheney a  bitter  horrible human being  look i've worked with liz uh i've said  all along that i don't think she should  be conference chair i was i was  you know what i'm driving at the former  president has language that is highly  personal at times  and insulting do you agree with any of  it in regards to liz cheney  well i think in this situation uh liz  has said some things about the president  i think it's probably  um elevated the the the rhetoric a  little bit  and sometimes he comes back that's  that's human nature i understand that  it's very sad yeah it is it's very very  sad to me what has happened to liz taney  that for telling the truth  something we all teach our children we  you tell the truth  she tells the truth and she is greatly  penalized for it  now there seems to be revisionist  history here in the republican party and  dare i say some selective amnesia about  what was said and what wasn't said well  i mean  to mr to congressman jordan's point that  this should be looked at it has been  the election should be looked at it has  been looked at it was taken to  i think 60 courts all of whom said  there's nothing here  and what's fascinating is elise stefanik  who will replace liz cheney presumably  has a much more moderate record of  voting in congress than liz cheney who  voted pretty much locked up with  president trump  no history is watching it will be  interesting to see how this all plays  out because i don't think it's over yet
 

